      "title": "Myanmar’s ousted leader Aung San Suu Kyi seen in rare photos after receiving gift from King Charles",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/20/myanmar-aung-san-suu-kyi-rare-photos-gift-king-charles",
      "description": "<p>Critics said images of detained former leader were a stunt by the military to end country’s diplomatic isolation</p><p>Myanmar has delivered presents from Britain’s ​King Charles to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/aung-san-suu-kyi\">Aung San Suu Kyi</a>, releasing rare photos of the imprisoned former leader in what critics said was a stunt by the country’s military to end diplomatic isolation.</p><p>A presidential spokesperson said <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/61590345011686/posts/122143435659344833/?mibextid=wwXIfr&amp;rdid=87EGEjBYeLatGeUb#\">on social media</a> that home ministry officials handed over two gardening books on soil, “along with one sealed envelope and a sealed diplomatic pouch”, from King Charles, who is known to have an interest in planting and the environment.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/20/myanmar-aung-san-suu-kyi-rare-photos-gift-king-charles\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
